# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.4.1) via npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Modified Files
**src/app/layout.tsx**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` element after the `{children}` element
- Preserved existing code structure and formatting

## Implementation Details
- Framework: Next.js 16.4.0 with App Router
- Documentation source: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart (fetched on 2026-10-13)
- Followed official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router implementation
- The Analytics component is placed in the root layout file for site-wide tracking

## Verification Steps Completed
✓ Build completed successfully (no TypeScript errors)
✓ Linter passed with no errors
✓ All existing functionality preserved
✓ Lock files properly updated

## Next Steps for Deployment
1. Commit and push these changes to your repository
2. Deploy to Vercel (the changes will be automatically deployed)
3. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel project dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project on Vercel
   - Go to the Analytics tab
   - Click the "Enable" button
4. After deployment, verify tracking is active by checking your browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`
5. View analytics data in your Vercel dashboard

## Notes
- The Analytics component requires no additional configuration
- It works seamlessly with Next.js routing and tracks page views automatically
- Data collection begins immediately upon deployment
- No environment variables or additional setup required
